<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:camunda="http://camunda.org/schema/1.0/bpmn" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_research" targetNamespace="http://codefrak.com/agent-army/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.51.1" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Platform" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="7.23.0">
  <bpmn:message id="message-research-filed" name="research filed" />
  <bpmn:process id="research" name="research" isExecutable="true" camunda:historyTimeToLive="180">
    <bpmn:documentation>The flow for a ticket of kind research (engine/README.md, "Research"): a research Smith answers the question in the ticket with answer.md and a self-contained answer.html page, asking the user through the question path when it must; the engine keeps the pair in engine.research_answer keyed by ticket and round and serves the page through GET /ticket/{owner}/{repo}/{n}/pitch, committing nothing; then it asks the asker for the ack (accept, save, drop, or a follow-up). A follow-up is the next round: the Smith runs again with the whole thread. Started by the issue scanner or POST /chore with kind research; an intake refined as research waits for its own authorized label.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start-research-filed" name="research filed">
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-start-answer</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_research" messageRef="message-research-filed" />
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="call-answer" name="answer the question&#10;(smith run)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" calledElement="reusable-smith-run">
      <bpmn:documentation>A research Smith on the ticket, at its tier: answers the question with answer.md and answer.html inline in result.json, citing what it read, changing no file and cutting no bundle; on round 2 and later the brief's research thread carries every earlier answer and the follow-ups; outcome answered or ask</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:in variables="all" />
        <camunda:in sourceExpression="${&#39;research&#39;}" target="mode" />
        <camunda:out variables="all" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-start-answer</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-answer-question</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-ack-follow-up</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-answer-outcome</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gateway-answer-outcome" name="outcome?">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-answer-outcome</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-answer-answered</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-answer-ask</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-post-question" name="post the smith&#39;s question&#10;(work item)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${postFeatureQuestion}">
      <bpmn:documentation>PostFeatureQuestionDelegate: records the research Smith's question in engine.intake_question and comments it on the ticket</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-answer-ask</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-question-answer</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="user-task-answer-question" name="answer the smith&#39;s question">
      <bpmn:documentation>Waits for POST /intake/{id}/answer from someone with research access; the answers join the brief of the next run</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-question-answer</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-answer-question</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-keep-answer" name="keep the answer&#10;(engine)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${keepAnswer}">
      <bpmn:documentation>KeepAnswerDelegate: the next round number; upserts answer.md and answer.html into engine.research_answer for the ticket and round, appends the round to the researchThread variable the next brief carries, and comments the summary with the round on the ticket; nothing is pushed</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-answer-answered</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-keep-ack</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-post-ack" name="ask for the ack&#10;(work item)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${postAck}">
      <bpmn:documentation>PostAckDelegate: records the ack question with its verbs in engine.intake_question (a decision in GET /needs) and comments it on the ticket with the summary and the round; after a refused save path it says why first</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-keep-ack</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-saved-refused</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-post-ack-answer</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="user-task-answer-decision" name="ack the answer">
      <bpmn:documentation>Waits for POST /intake/{id}/answer from someone with research access: accept, save, drop, or anything else as a follow-up question</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-post-ack-answer</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-answer-read</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-read-ack" name="read the ack" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${readAck}">
      <bpmn:documentation>ReadAckDelegate: the last answer read by Jev (use case research-decision) and AckVerb into decision (accept, save, drop or follow-up), decisionWhy and decidedBy; a pick below the floor, no Jev answer or an unreadable answer is a follow-up, never a re-ask</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-answer-read</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-read-ack</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gateway-ack" name="verb?" default="flow-ack-follow-up">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-read-ack</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-ack-accept</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-ack-save</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-ack-drop</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-ack-follow-up</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-save-answer" name="save to the repo&#10;(git)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${saveAnswer}">
      <bpmn:documentation>SaveAnswerDelegate: one commit by the engine's identity on the default branch adding &lt;dir&gt;/&lt;yyyy-mm-dd&gt;-&lt;slug&gt;.md and .html (dir from the answer, default bots/research/; must be under bots/research/ or docs/), commented on the ticket; a path outside them is refused with a comment and saved is false</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-ack-save</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-save-outcome</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gateway-saved" name="saved?">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-save-outcome</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-saved-close</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-saved-refused</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-close-accepted" name="close completed&#10;(work item)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${closeResearch}">
      <bpmn:documentation>CloseResearchDelegate: comments the decision (and the commit, after a save) on the ticket and closes it as completed</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-ack-accept</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-saved-close</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-accepted-end</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="task-close-dropped" name="close not planned&#10;(work item)" camunda:asyncBefore="true" camunda:delegateExpression="${closeResearch}">
      <bpmn:documentation>CloseResearchDelegate: comments the decision on the ticket and closes it as not planned</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-ack-drop</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow-dropped-end</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end-research-decided" name="research decided">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-accepted-end</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow-dropped-end</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-start-answer" sourceRef="start-research-filed" targetRef="call-answer" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-answer-outcome" sourceRef="call-answer" targetRef="gateway-answer-outcome" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-answer-answered" name="answered" sourceRef="gateway-answer-outcome" targetRef="task-keep-answer">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${outcome == 'answered'}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-answer-ask" name="ask" sourceRef="gateway-answer-outcome" targetRef="task-post-question">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${outcome == 'ask'}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-question-answer" sourceRef="task-post-question" targetRef="user-task-answer-question" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-answer-question" sourceRef="user-task-answer-question" targetRef="call-answer" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-keep-ack" sourceRef="task-keep-answer" targetRef="task-post-ack" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-post-ack-answer" sourceRef="task-post-ack" targetRef="user-task-answer-decision" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-answer-read" sourceRef="user-task-answer-decision" targetRef="task-read-ack" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-read-ack" sourceRef="task-read-ack" targetRef="gateway-ack" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-ack-accept" name="accept" sourceRef="gateway-ack" targetRef="task-close-accepted">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${decision == 'accept'}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-ack-save" name="save" sourceRef="gateway-ack" targetRef="task-save-answer">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${decision == 'save'}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-ack-drop" name="drop" sourceRef="gateway-ack" targetRef="task-close-dropped">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${decision == 'drop'}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-ack-follow-up" name="follow-up: next round" sourceRef="gateway-ack" targetRef="call-answer" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-save-outcome" sourceRef="task-save-answer" targetRef="gateway-saved" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-saved-close" name="saved" sourceRef="gateway-saved" targetRef="task-close-accepted">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${saved}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-saved-refused" name="path refused: ask again" sourceRef="gateway-saved" targetRef="task-post-ack">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">${!saved}</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-accepted-end" sourceRef="task-close-accepted" targetRef="end-research-decided" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow-dropped-end" sourceRef="task-close-dropped" targetRef="end-research-decided" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="annotation-engine-kept">
      <bpmn:text>the page is kept by the engine and served through the pitch endpoint, never committed unless the asker says save. engine/readme.md, "research"</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="association-engine-kept" sourceRef="task-keep-answer" targetRef="annotation-engine-kept" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_research">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_research" bpmnElement="research">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="start-research-filed-di" bpmnElement="start-research-filed">
